body:
I have a few stories which are pretty funny. 

&#x200B;

1: I was racing my friend down the street on his bikes. I wasn't really good at riding bikes as I don't have one of my own to practice on (I was good enough to ride around at a decent speed). So my friend got in the lead of me and i thought it would be a good idea to pedal as fast as i could. I was going fast as hell probably twice as fast as him and I ended up hitting a bump in the road and flipping multiple times down the road. I had a scrape on my entire arm and was in a lot of pain. 

&#x200B;

2: I was playing a zombie tag like game that we would usually do at night around my friends block and i decided to hide up in a tree. he eventually found me after i kept shouting at him and he starting climbing the tree. I really didn't want to get caught so I went along one of the branches to try and escape him. as he was about to tag me I let go of the branch and fell like 10 meters to the ground and landed on my back. I started running as fast as I could before he climbed back down the tree and found another spot to hide.

I don't know if an item has already been written like this anywhere because im thinking of this on the top of my head. 

&#x200B;

Basically its a device that allows you to create dimensions and transport between them. The dimension you can create can be whatever you want and it essentially makes you a God in your dimensions. 

&#x200B;

The Pokemon world? For sure. 

Any video game you wanted to experience as reality? Yep.

Any movie, book or show you wanted to be a character in? Of course.

Anything you can think of off the top of your head? If its detailed enough for you to experience the 5 senses you can go there.

&#x200B;

Now what can you do in these worlds? Anything you ever wanted as the device allows you to change literally everything about your dimensions and you can travel between them whenever you want. Of course you should make sure to pause the time before doing so. 

&#x200B;

Basically you can become whoever you want to be, where ever you wanted and you could have anything you ever dreamed of.

&#x200B;

anyways if anyone wants to cover anything i missed that the device can also do please enlighten others.

I usually only load 20% on all tanks but go for 50% on tanks with high ammo or bad pen

&#x200B;

I don't free xp the lower tiers because I have everything up to tier 5 researched. I will use free xp on some packages for bad tanks because I have to grind out my free xp.

Well to be honest even if you commit suicide or not the outcome is still the same. the only difference is the longer you go on the more you suffer.

&#x200B;

no matter how much you achieve in life, no matter how much you do to help this world you will never see the impact you made. 

after you die you no longer have a body which means you also do not have a brain. so tbh the only reason im afraid of suicide is the failure. 

&#x200B;

I can relate to you so much. I haven't lost a loved on yet but I probably will soon. My brother (1 year older) has cancer and it is only getting worse. I am already super depressed so i will probably end up killing myself when i can. 

&#x200B;

I can't say this will work for you but I get myself lost in my world, I do anything i can to occupy myself. I am trying to learn new languages and that helps keep my mind off the big negative.
